  "body": "Supersedes #2036\n\nGitHub closed #2036 when its parent #2023 merged and its base branch was deleted. This PR has the same branch.\n\n## Merge of main\n\n- `git merge origin/main` was clean (no conflicts, no hand edits in the merge).\n- The fix commit cfadf347b wrote `crates/ui/src/interact.rs` with CRLF line ends. The diff showed each line of that file as changed. Commit 6a800e5ce restores LF. The content does not change. The diff of `interact.rs` against main is now 14 lines added and 2 lines removed.\n- Main does not compile `camcraft-ui` at this time: `crates/ui/src/machine_modes.rs` `short_caption` has no arm for `MachineKind::Waterjet` (E0004). This PR does not fix that. For the test run, I added the arm locally and did not commit it.\n\n## What changed\n- The world gizmo draws only the axes that the machine has.\n- A mill shows X, Y and Z.\n- A lathe shows Z and X. It shows Y only when its machine file states a linear Y axis.\n- A mill-turn keeps the milling frame, as #2023 does. It hides Y only when its file states axes and none is a linear Y. An unstated axis list hides nothing.\n- The change reuses the view frame of #2023. There is no second derivation of the lathe orientation. The new `view_frame::axes_shown` only filters the axis lines and the axis letters.\n- Display only. The WCS, the toolpaths and the posted G-code do not read it.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2019-lathe-gizmo.md` (mill-turn rule).\n\n## Screenshots (offscreen, 1280x800)\nBefore (Y axis drawn on a lathe):\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/cc3a8de149ae431f676678061599bc7885aff9e1/pr-2019/lathe-gizmo-before.png\n\nAfter (X up, Z to the right, no Y):\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/cc3a8de149ae431f676678061599bc7885aff9e1/pr-2019/lathe-gizmo-after.png\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/lathe_gizmo.rs`)\n- `a_mill_shows_x_y_and_z`\n- `a_lathe_without_y_shows_z_and_x_only`\n- `a_lathe_with_a_y_axis_shows_y_too`\n- `a_mill_again_brings_y_back`\n- `the_mill_turn_rule_keeps_the_milling_frame_and_follows_the_y_axis`\n\nResult on 6a800e5ce (with the local Waterjet arm): the 5 pinning tests pass. The filters also pass: `law_tests` (69), `axis_note` (2), `wcs_gizmo` (1), `structural` (15), `lathe_` (18). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- A test that the posted program of a turning golden is unchanged. The gizmo code does not read the post path. The test pins only that no command enters the history.\n- View cube face names for the lathe frame. The cube names world directions and #2023 keeps them true. No change was needed.\n- Pixel snapshots (release lane). No PNG golden changed.\n- The screenshots are from the old head. The merge of main did not change the gizmo code.\n\nChangelog: The world gizmo hides the Y axis on a lathe that has no Y axis.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2019\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
